| V1 Niagara User Array positive path | FAIL | Array payload did not reach a usable Niagara user array. Set/get length stayed `0/0`; no RT stamp proof. |
| V2 PhysMat BP fixture | BLOCKED | Temp PhysicalMaterials and overrides worked, but no BP/native `bReturnPhysicalMaterial=true` result was available. |
| V3 Footprint mask texture stamp | BLOCKED | Deterministic mask Texture2D import works through the guarded importer, but Texture2D DI binding and `SampleTexture2D` stage authoring are missing. |
| V5 Previous-frame temporal alignment | BLOCKED | Previous-grid API existence remains proven, but exact previous-frame timing was not measured. |
| V4 Deterministic reprojection | BLOCKED | General User param upsert and Custom HLSL wrapper work, but no dedicated reprojection stage/readback exists. |
| V6 Pose freshness | BLOCKED | Piper foot bones are confirmed; animated PrePhysics/PostUpdateWork fixture is still missing. |

## Important Corrections From This Round

General Niagara User parameters are not the blocker:

- `User.V1_Count` as `int32`: upsert PASS.
- `User.V4_DeltaUV` as `Vector2D`: upsert PASS.
- Custom HLSL wrapping of `StackContext.RGBA` with those User inputs: PASS.

The real remaining blockers are:

- User Array Data Interface creation/upsert.
- Niagara Array Get/Count loop authoring in a simulation stage.
- Texture2D Data Interface binding.
- `SampleTexture2D` rotated footprint mask stage authoring.
- Frame-counter temporal probe authoring.
- Dedicated deterministic reprojection stage authoring.
- PhysMat trace fixture returning `PhysicalMaterial`.
- Live animated pose freshness fixture.

## V1. Niagara User Array Positive Path

Result: FAIL

Temporary asset:

```text
/Game/_MCP_Temp/ReactiveGhost2/NS_V1_ArrayStamp
```

Measured evidence:

- G1 template duplication succeeded.
- `inspect_niagara_user_parameters`: `parameter_count=0`, `settable_count=0`.
- UE Python exposes several array DI classes:
  - `NiagaraDataInterfaceArrayPosition`: constructable.
  - `NiagaraDataInterfaceArrayFloat`: constructable.
  - `NiagaraDataInterfaceArrayInt32`: constructable.
  - `NiagaraDataInterfaceArrayVector`: not exposed by that exact name.
- Python `NiagaraSystem.get_exposed_parameters()` was not available.
- `SetNiagaraArrayVector(User.V1_Positions, 3 values)` then get returned length `0`.
- `SetNiagaraArrayFloat(User.V1_Strengths, 3 values)` then get returned length `0`.
- Editor log reported:

```text
OverrideParameter(User.V1_Positions) System(NS_V1_ArrayStamp) DataInterface(NiagaraDataInterfaceArrayFloat3) was not found
OverrideParameter(User.V1_Strengths) System(NS_V1_ArrayStamp) DataInterface(NiagaraDataInterfaceArrayFloat) was not found
```

Additional correction:

- `upsert_niagara_user_parameters` can create scalar/vector User parameters.
- `User.V1_Count int32` upsert succeeded.
- Custom HLSL wrapper using `User.V1_Count` succeeded.
- Therefore V1 failed specifically at User Array DI creation and Array Get/Count loop authoring, not at scalar User parameter support.

Document update:

```text
§10.3: Do not finalize array source registry as the Phase 1/2 source path. First implementation should use fixed explicit slots or InteractionField-style fixed-slot expansion. Promote array registry only after User Array DI creation/upsert, Niagara Array Get/Count loop, Count gate, and RT readback all pass.
```

